  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "Let's walk the deflation spiral one step at a time, because each rung quietly makes the next one worse.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "props": [
            "chartDown",
            "clock"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Prices fall.",
            "Then what?"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "First, shoppers delay. Then sales drop. Then firms cut wages and jobs. Then people spend even less, and prices fall again.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "rows",
          "kicker": "The deflation spiral",
          "rows": [
            {
              "rank": "1",
              "name": "Buyers wait",
              "value": "↓",
              "note": "it'll be cheaper later",
              "color": "#5c544c",
              "bar": 0.25
            },
            {
              "rank": "2",
              "name": "Sales fall",
              "value": "↓",
              "note": "revenue dries up",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.5
            },
            {
              "rank": "3",
              "name": "Wages & jobs cut",
              "value": "↓",
              "note": "incomes shrink",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.75
            },
            {
              "rank": "4",
              "name": "Spend even less",
              "value": "↺",
              "note": "and it loops",
              "color": "#c0392b",
              "bar": 1.0
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "That self-reinforcing fall in the price level is textbook deflation.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-deflation",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · deflation"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Economists even have a name for the core problem. Saving feels smart for you, but it's a disaster for everyone at once.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "kicker": "the paradox",
          "line": "Paradox of thrift",
          "sub": "good for one, bad for all"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "When everyone saves at once, total demand collapses.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-thrift",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · paradox of thrift"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And central banks lose their main tool, because rates can't fall much below zero.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "bank",
          "big": "below 0%",
          "label": "the number they fear",
          "props": [
            "x",
            "chartDown"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "That dead end is known as a liquidity trap.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-trap",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · liquidity trap"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "We have watched this exact spiral play out before, in the nineteen thirties.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "red",
          "line": "We've seen it",
          "props": [
            "clock",
            "chartDown"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The Great Depression was deflation doing its very worst.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-depression",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · Great Depression"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Have you seen any of these rungs playing out around you?",
